  "conclusion": "Temporal source identity is controlled by separation between dynamical signatures relative to finite-window estimation noise, not rank alone. Static PCA preserves the full source subspace but not source axes. One-lag AMUSE is as good as or better than the conservative multi-lag operator for pure AR(1), where extra lags are redundant. Exact equal AR signatures retain a rotational ambiguity even as the degenerate two-dimensional subspace converges to nearly perfect recovery. Time shuffling destroys source identity while leaving the subspace intact. At higher rank, small per-axis errors accumulate enough that component labels can look mostly correct while the full reusable transfer map still fails."
